  "body": {
    "id": "thm:finite-menu-higbee-contrast",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For the theorem-level comparison, \\(\\mathfrak C_{\\mathrm H}\\) is the class of two-wave policy-design problems with a continuously parameterized action \\(\\gamma\\in\\Gamma_{\\mathrm H}\\), local state \\(h\\in\\mathcal U_{\\mathrm H}\\), and population welfare \\(W_{\\mathrm H}(h,\\gamma)\\) satisfying the following maintained conditions: \\(W_{\\mathrm H}\\) is twice continuously differentiable in \\(\\gamma\\) on a relative neighborhood of its optimizer graph; for every \\(h\\in\\mathcal U_{\\mathrm H}\\), \\(\\operatorname*{argmax}_{\\gamma\\in\\Gamma_{\\mathrm H}}W_{\\mathrm H}(h,\\gamma)\\) is a singleton in \\(\\operatorname{relint}(\\Gamma_{\\mathrm H})\\); and \\(-\\nabla_{\\gamma}^2W_{\\mathrm H}(h,\\gamma)\\succeq c_{\\mathrm H}I_{s_{\\mathrm H}}\\) on that neighborhood for one \\(c_{\\mathrm H}>0\\). At \\(\\omega_0\\), the finite-menu choice correspondence at \\(h=0\\) is \\(\\operatorname*{argmax}_{j\\in[3]}h_j=[3]\\), with \\(h_3=0\\), and every relative neighborhood of \\(0\\) in \\(\\mathcal H=[-1,1]^2\\) contains states at which each labeled policy is uniquely welfare maximizing. If an instance of \\(\\mathfrak C_{\\mathrm H}\\) preserved the three labeled choices through an injective map \\(\\iota_{\\mathrm H}:[3]\\to\\Gamma_{\\mathrm H}\\), in the explicit sense that \\(\\operatorname*{argmax}_{\\gamma\\in\\Gamma_{\\mathrm H}}W_{\\mathrm H}(h,\\gamma)=\\{\\iota_{\\mathrm H}(j):j\\in\\operatorname*{argmax}_{k\\in[3]}h_k\\}\\) for every \\(h\\in\\mathcal U_{\\mathrm H}\\), then at \\(h=0\\) its optimizer set would contain the three distinct points \\(\\iota_{\\mathrm H}(1),\\iota_{\\mathrm H}(2),\\iota_{\\mathrm H}(3)\\), directly contradicting the maintained singleton condition. Thus the rational witness is outside \\(\\mathfrak C_{\\mathrm H}\\) because its three-way tie fails uniqueness. Moreover, with \\(K=4\\), \\(L=3\\), and \\(d=2\\), the selectively observed model has \\(2K(L-1)-d=14\\) contrast-preserving nuisance coordinates, and projecting them by \\(\\Pi_r\\) yields the design-dependent non-diagonal efficient covariance \\(\\Sigma(r)\\). Higbee's smooth unique-optimum comparator therefore covers neither the witness's finite-menu tie geometry nor its selective-annotation nuisance step.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(\\omega_0\\)",
      "\\(h\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal H\\)",
      "\\(\\mathfrak C_{\\mathrm H}\\)",
      "\\(\\gamma\\)",
