      "thm:gaussian-value-characterization"
    ],
    "justification": "The theorem isolates both obstructions to importing smooth unique-optimum policy-design theory: a genuine three-way local tie and an observation-design-dependent nuisance projection.",
    "gap": "Higbee (2026) derives two-wave policy design under a unique, strongly concave smooth policy optimum; the finite-menu tie geometry and selective-annotation nuisance experiment in this theorem lie outside those assumptions.",
    "consumer": "The result tells the attainment proof exactly which smooth argmax and direct-policy-observation reductions are unavailable at the rational witness.",
    "proof_tex": "The first paragraph of the claim is exactly the defining list of member properties of \\(\\mathfrak C_{\\mathrm H}\\). At \\(\\omega_0\\), \\(h_3=0\\) and \\(h=(0,0)\\) gives equal welfare to all three labels, so the finite-menu argmax is \\([3]\\). Every relative neighborhood of zero in \\([-1,1]^2\\) contains, respectively, points with \\(h_1>\\max(h_2,0)\\), with \\(h_2>\\max(h_1,0)\\), and with \\(0>\\max(h_1,h_2)\\); hence each policy is uniquely optimal arbitrarily close to the tie.\n\nIf the asserted injective representation existed, evaluation at \\(h=0\\) would give the optimizer set \\(\\{\\iota_{\\mathrm H}(1),\\iota_{\\mathrm H}(2),\\iota_{\\mathrm H}(3)\\}\\). Injectivity makes these three points distinct, contradicting the singleton condition in the definition of \\(\\mathfrak C_{\\mathrm H}\\). Thus no smooth unique-optimum instance preserves this labelled choice correspondence.\n\nThe nuisance dimension is obtained directly from the saturated tangent:\n\\[\n2K(L-1)-d=2\\cdot4\\cdot2-2=14.\n\\]\nBy \\(\\mathrm{lem:efficient\\text{-}contrast\\text{-}information}\\), projection through \\(\\Pi_r\\) produces \\(\\Sigma(r)\\). At the witness, stratum three has \\(d_3=(1,1)^\\top\\), so its strictly positive contribution has a positive off-diagonal entry; hence the covariance is design-dependent and non-diagonal. These are respectively the tie-geometry and selective-observation obstructions claimed.",
